<h1>Localiser Performance Check</h1>
<div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;" align="center">
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3"></div>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Localiser Performance Check is a quick test to confirm that the localiser performance is within specification.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The alignment block supplied with the ModelMaker system comes with a conical hole designed for this test. If the block is not available, the ideal dimensions for a cone to be used with a 6mm diameter ball probe is diameter 8mm x 45 degrees. The ModelMaker sensor does not have to be in place for this test.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">Performance Check Procedure</span></h2>
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:10pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Ensure the localiser hardware and software setup is complete.</font></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">The block should be mounted in the position shown in the diagram. The distance between localiser and block will depend on the localiser type. For an 8' FARO arm it is approximately 500mm (50mm).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img id="_x0000_i1026" src="../images/arm_cube.jpg" width="320px" height="178px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></span></p>
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Run KUBE</span> <span lang="EN-GB">software.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Select <b>Dynamic Point Capture</b> button <img src="../images/capture_dynamic_points.gif" width="27px" height="27px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""> from the toolbar or</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Scan Data &gt; Capture &gt; Dynamic Points</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">from the menu.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<table class="MsoNormalTable" style="mso-cellspacing:0in; mso-padding-alt:0in 0in 0in 0in; border-spacing:0px; margin-left:36px;" cellspacing="0">
<col>
<col>
<tr class="whs7">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" height="38" class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB"><img id="_x0000_i1027" src="../images/single_hole_check1.jpg" width="120px" height="120px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td height="38" class="whs8">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Start capturing points.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Rotate the probe for 360 degrees.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Stop capturing points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs10">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" height="78" class="whs11">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB"><img id="_x0000_i1028" src="../images/single_hole_check2.jpg" width="120px" height="120px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td height="78" class="whs11">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Flip the probe to the opposite position (approximately 135 degrees).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
<tr class="whs12">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" height="38" class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB"><img id="_x0000_i1029" src="../images/single_hole_check3.jpg" width="120px" height="120px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td height="38" class="whs8">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Start capturing points.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Rotate the probe for 360 degrees.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Stop capturing points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Select all points.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">From the menu select <b>Fit Single Point</b> function (</span><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Measure &gt; Geometry &gt; Point</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check the results:</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="../images/fit_point.jpg" width="215px" height="363px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Statistics figures should be less than 3 Sigma.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The value of 3 Sigma will depend on which FARO arm is being used. This value can be calculated by multiplying 2 Sigma (found on the FARO arm) by 1.5.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">For example: 2 Sigma = 0.051 =&gt; 3 Sigma = 0.076</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img id="_x0000_i1031" src="../images/faro_sticker.jpg" width="320px" height="240px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">What to do if the results are outside the specification</span></h2>
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Repeat the performance check if a large error is observed. It is possible that the ball probe may not have been seated correctly in the cone.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Ensure the localiser is moved slowly during dynamic points capture with the probe firmly placed in the cone. If the results are again outside specification, check the localiser performance using the manufacturer's procedure e.g FARO arm ball bar test.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
